  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh Climate Change Resilience Fund - Initiative Climate Change</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Bangladesh Climate Change Resilience Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">By 2020 the BCCRF will be a government led, owned, and managed collaborative and sustainableclimate change financing mechanism, which is transparent and accountable, aimed at developingcapacity and resilience of the country to meet the challenges of climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Givargemensam fond (MDTF) som administreras av V&#xe4;rldsbanken. Syftet   &#xe4;r att st&#xf6;dja implementeringen av Bangladesh egen klimatstrategi.     &#xd6;vriga givare &#xe4;r Dfid, EU-delegationen och Danmark.Sveriges bidrag    h&#xe4;rr&#xf6;r fr&#xe5;n regeringens s&#xe4;rskilda klimatsatsning f&#xf6;r 2009-2012.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Bank Multi Donor Trust Fund for CC adapt. The objective with    Bangladesh Climate Change Resilience Fund (BCCRF) is to contribute to the implementation of Bangladesh Climate Change Strategy and Action   Plan, Other contributing donors to BCCRF are DfID, the EU-delegation, and Denmark.The Swedish support comes from the CC Initiative. The     World Bank has been appointed as trustee and fund administrator.</narrative>
  </description>
